# SHACL closure for Exercise 7.
#
# The topo-line block imported from the topo-feature register carries rules (topo-refs-exist.shacl)
# requiring every feature a topology references to exist in the graph being validated, and to have a
# Point geometry. The example line references P1 and P2 by id but - being a minimal example - does not
# define them.
#
# This file supplies them. It is merged into the example's RDF graph before SHACL validation runs, but
# is not part of the example data itself. Each stub carries only what the imported rules check: a Point
# geometry, with the coordinates that topo-feature's geometry rules require of every Point.
#
# The IRIs must match the example's `base-uri` in examples.yaml, which the relative ids "P1" and "P2"
# resolve against during semantic uplift. They are deliberately specific to this exercise, so they
# cannot collide with ids defined by other examples.

@prefix geojson: <https://purl.org/geojson/vocab#> .

<https://example.org/bblocks-tutorial/exercise7/P1> a geojson:Feature ;
    geojson:geometry [ a geojson:Point ; geojson:coordinates ( 0 0 ) ] .

<https://example.org/bblocks-tutorial/exercise7/P2> a geojson:Feature ;
    geojson:geometry [ a geojson:Point ; geojson:coordinates ( 1 1 ) ] .
